[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:11. Not Guilty]
[00:00.620] Passage 11 | 第11课
[00:02.025] Not guilty. | 无罪。
[00:04.085] Going through the customs is a tiresome business. | 过海关是一件麻烦事。
[00:07.815] The strangest thing about it is that really honest people | 最奇怪的是，那些真正诚实的人
[00:11.600] are often made to feel guilty. | 常常会觉得自己有罪。
[00:13.630] The hardened professional smuggler, on the other hand, | 而那些老练的职业走私犯，
[00:16.790] is never troubled by such feelings, | 却从不为此感到困扰，
[00:18.840] even if he has 500 gold watches hidden in his suitcase. | 即使他的手提箱里藏着500块金表。
[00:23.080] When I returned from abroad recently, | 最近我从国外回来时，
[00:25.725] a particularly officious young customs officer | 一位特别爱管闲事的年轻海关官员，
[00:28.845] clearly regarded me as a smuggler. | 显然把我当成了走私犯。
[00:31.470] "Have you anything to declare?" | “你有什么要申报的吗？”
[00:33.865] he asked, | 他问，
[00:34.805] looking me in the eye. | 眼睛直勾勾地盯着我。
[00:36.820] "No," | “没有，”
[00:37.980] I answered confidently. | 我自信地回答。
[00:39.925] "Would you mind unlocking this suitcase, please?" | “请你打开这个手提箱好吗？”
[00:43.795] "Not at all," | “没问题，”
[00:45.044] I answered. | 我回答。
[00:46.335] The officer went through the case with great care. | 官员非常仔细地检查了箱子。
[00:49.780] All the things I'd packed so carefully were soon in a dreadful mess. | 我精心打包的所有东西很快就变得一团糟。
[00:53.790] I felt sure I would never be able to close the case again. | 我确信我再也关不上这个箱子了。
[00:57.440] Suddenly, | 突然，
[00:58.835] I saw the official's face light up. | 我看到那位官员的脸上露出了喜色。
[01:01.550] He had spotted a tiny bottle at the bottom of my case, | 他在我的箱子底部发现了一个小瓶子，
[01:05.870] and he pounced on it with delight. | 他高兴地扑了过去。
[01:08.830] "Perfume, eh?" | “香水，嗯？”
[01:11.460] he asked sarcastically. | 他嘲讽地问道。
[01:13.850] "You should have declared that. | “你应该申报的。
[01:16.285] Perfume is not exempt from import duty." | 香水不在免税商品之列。”
[01:20.400] "But it isn't perfume," | “但这不是香水，”
[01:22.407] I said. | 我说。
[01:23.090] "It's hair oil." | “是发油。”
[01:24.980] Then I added with a smile, | 接着我微笑着补充道，
[01:27.310] "It's a strange mixture I make myself." | “这是一种我自制的奇怪混合物。”
[01:31.150] As I expected, | 正如我所料，
[01:33.190] he did not believe me. | 他不相信我。
[01:35.345] "Try it!" | “试试看！”
[01:36.690] I said encouragingly. | 我鼓励地说。
[01:38.480] The officer unscrewed the cap and put the bottle to his nostrils. | 官员拧开瓶盖，把瓶子凑到鼻孔前。
[01:42.805] He was greeted by an unpleasant smell which convinced him that I was telling the truth. | 一股难闻的气味扑鼻而来，这让他相信我说的是实话。
[01:48.340] A few minutes later, I was able to hurry away with precious chalk marks on my baggage. | 几分钟后，我得以匆匆离去，行李上盖有珍贵的粉笔标记。